 content\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"dl\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFacts__31L_R\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_kvRow__4UVrC\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactKey__u_Yuk\",\"children\":\"Closed before review\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactVal___yIlQ u-mono u-tnum\",\"children\":\"2,329\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_kvRow__4UVrC\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactKey__u_Yuk\",\"children\":\"Read by an analyst\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactVal___yIlQ u-mono u-tnum\",\"children\":\"518\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_kvRow__4UVrC\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"dt\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactKey__u_Yuk\",\"children\":\"Total signal\"}],[\"$\",\"dd\",null,{\"className\":\"product_gaugeFactVal___yIlQ u-mono u-tnum\",\"children\":\"2,847\"}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_breakdownCell__8Ggr_\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"product_sectionLabel__iRUDV\",\"children\":[\"By severity — \",\"24 h to 2026-10-14 14:31 UTC\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_breakdown__cbxRc\",\"role\":\"table\",\"aria-label\":\"Alert count by severity\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"product_head__PTccq\",\"role\":\"row\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"product_headCell__m8m1J\",\"role\":\"columnheader\",\"children\":\"Severity\"}],\"$L88\",\"$L89\",\"$L8a\"]}],[\"$L8b\",\"$L8c\",\"$L8d\",\"$L8e\",\"$L8f\"]]}],\"$L90\"]}]]}],\"$L91\"]}],\"$L92\"]}]}]]}]\n49:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"dg dg-scope\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeIn\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeTag u-mono\",\"children\":[\"Inside the boundary\",[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCount\",\"children\":\"6 surfaces\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeGrid\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"Web application testing\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"Web application testing\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"Authenticated and unauthenticated, per-role. Business-logic abuse, not just the OWASP list — the flaws that matter are usually in what your application is allowed to do, not in how it parses input.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"API testing\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"02\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"API testing\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"REST, GraphQL and gRPC against the spec and against reality. Object-level and function-level authorisation are where we find the most, and they are what scanners find least.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Mobile application testing\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"03\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"Mobile application testing\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"iOS and Android binaries, runtime instrumentation with Frida, certificate pinning bypass, local storage and keychain review, plus the backend the app actually talks to.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Internal and network testing\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"04\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"Internal and network testing\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"From an assumed-breach position on the corporate LAN or a VPN foothold. Active Directory path analysis, lateral movement, credential exposure, and the service accounts nobody has rotated since 2019.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Cloud configuration review\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"05\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"Cloud configuration review\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"AWS, Azure and GCP. IAM trust-policy analysis, exposed storage, metadata-service access from compute, and the cross-account roles your CI uses.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"Retest as standard\",{\"className\":\"dg-scopeCell\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"u-mono dg-scopeNum\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":\"06\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeName\",\"children\":\"Retest as standard\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeBody\",\"children\":\"A full retest of every finding within 30 days of the report, included. Fixes get verified or they get reopened with evidence.\"}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"aside\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeOut\",\"aria-label\":\"Outside the boundary\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeTag dg-scopeTag--out u-mono\",\"children\":\"Outside the boundary\"}],[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeOutQ\",\"children\":\"What is not included?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-scopeOutA\",\"children\":\"Denial-of-service testing, physical intrusion, and social engineering of your staff are out of scope unless separately agreed — the first because it proves little and risks much, the other two because they belong in a red team engagement with different rules. Remediation work is also separate: we will tell you exactly what to change, and our engineering practice can do it, but a tester who fixes their own findings cannot retest them impartially.\"}]]}]]}]\n4b:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"dg\",\"id\":\"engagement-shape\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-gantt\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 1000 252\",\"preserveAspectRatio\":\"xMidYMid meet\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"Engagement shape for Penetration Testing: 6 phases. Phase 1, Scoping, 3–5 days before start, before the window opens. Phase 2, Reconnaissance and mapping, Day 1, inside the engagement window. Phase 3, Manual testing, Days 2–8, inside the engagement window. Phase 4, Reporting, Days 9–11, inside the engagement window, producing the technical report. Phase 5, Debrief, Within 5 days of the report, after the report, producing the 90-minute debrief with the testers. Phase 6, Retest, Within 30 days, after the report, producing the retest report within 30 days with a per-finding verified status.\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-axisUnit\",\"x\":0,\"y\":16,\"children\":\"weeks from kick-off\"}],[[\"$\",\"g\",\"0\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":290.5652173913044,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":290.5652173913044,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":290.5652173913044,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":\"$-0\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":443.3478260869565,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":443.3478260869565,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":443.3478260869565,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":2}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-grid\",\"x1\":596.1304347826087,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":596.1304347826087,\"y2\":226}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-tick\",\"x\":596.1304347826087,\"y\":24,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":4}]]}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-zero\",\"x1\":290.5652173913044,\"y1\":30,\"x2\":290.5652173913044,\"y2\":232}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-zeroLabel\",\"x\":290.5652173913044,\"y\":245,\"textAnchor\":\"middle\",\"children\":\"kick-off\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-colHead\",\"x\":762,\"y\":16,\"children\":\"Drops out\"}],[[\"$\",\"g\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":65,\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":65,\"children\":\"Scoping\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--before\",\"x\":236,\"y\":53.5,\"width\":54.56521739130437,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":298.5652173913044,\"y\":64,\"children\":\"3–5 days before start\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":64,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"2\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":95,\"children\":\"02\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":95,\"children\":\"Reconnaissance and mapping\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":290.5652173913044,\"y\":83.5,\"width\":10.913043478260875,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":309.47826086956525,\"y\":94,\"children\":\"Day 1\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":94,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"3\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":125,\"children\":\"03\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":125,\"children\":\"Manual testing\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":301.47826086956525,\"y\":113.5,\"width\":76.39130434782601,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":385.86956521739125,\"y\":124,\"children\":\"Days 2–8\"}]],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artNone\",\"x\":771,\"y\":124,\"children\":\"—\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"4\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":155,\"children\":\"04\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":155,\"children\":\"Reporting\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--window\",\"x\":377.86956521739125,\"y\":143.5,\"width\":32.73913043478262,\"height\":15,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":418.6086956521739,\"y\":154,\"children\":\"Days 9–11\"}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-leader\",\"x1\":748,\"y1\":151,\"x2\":757,\"y2\":151}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artMark\",\"x\":757,\"y\":147,\"width\":8,\"height\":8,\"rx\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-art\",\"x\":771,\"y\":154,\"children\":\"Technical report\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"5\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":185,\"children\":\"05\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":185,\"children\":\"Debrief\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--after\",\"x\":410.6086956521739,\"y\":177,\"width\":54.56521739130437,\"height\":8,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":473.17391304347825,\"y\":184,\"children\":\"Within 5 days of the…\"}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-leader\",\"x1\":748,\"y1\":181,\"x2\":757,\"y2\":181}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artMark\",\"x\":757,\"y\":177,\"width\":8,\"height\":8,\"rx\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-art\",\"x\":771,\"y\":184,\"children\":\"90-minute debrief with the te…\"}]]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"6\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowNum\",\"x\":0,\"y\":215,\"children\":\"06\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-rowName\",\"x\":34,\"y\":215,\"children\":\"Retest\"}],[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-bar dg-bar--after\",\"x\":410.6086956521739,\"y\":207,\"width\":327.3913043478261,\"height\":8,\"rx\":2}],null,[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-barLabel\",\"x\":402.6086956521739,\"y\":214,\"textAnchor\":\"end\",\"children\":\"Within 30 days\"}]],[[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-leader\",\"x1\":748,\"y1\":211,\"x2\":757,\"y2\":211}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-artMark\",\"x\":757,\"y\":207,\"width\":8,\"height\":8,\"rx\":1}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-art\",\"x\":771,\"y\":214,\"children\":\"Retest report within 30 days…\"}]]]}]]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-ganttText\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sched\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"dg-schedRow\",\"data-stage\":\"before\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-schedHead\",\"children\":[\"$L93\",\"$L94\"]}],\"$L95\",\"$L96\",\"$L97\"]}],\"$L98\",\"$L99\",\"$L9a\",\"$L9b\",\"$L9c\"]}]}],\"$L9d\"]}]\n9e:Tc1d,\n/* ---- Chapter ------------------------------------------------------------\n   A numbered chapter with a heading that HOLDS while its body scrolls under\n   it. The number is not decoration: it tells a reader where they are in a long\n   page, which is the thing a long page actually owes them. */\n.ch {\n  position: relative;\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s8);\n}\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .ch {\n    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr);\n    gap: var(--s16);\n    align-items: start;\n  }\n}\n\n.ch__head {\n  position: relative;\n}\n@media (min-width: 1024px) {\n  .ch__head {\n    position: sticky;\n    /* Clears the fixed 72px nav plus breathing room. */\n    top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s8));\n  }\n}\n\n.ch__num {\n  display: block;\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  letter-spacing: 0.18em;\n  color: var(--accent);\n  margin-bottom: var(--s3);\n}\n\n.ch__title {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.4vw, var(--text-4xl));\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n  text-wrap: balance;\n}\n\n.ch__lede {\n  margin: var(--s4) 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  font-size: var(--text-base);\n  line-height: 1.6;\n  max-width: 34ch;\n}\n\n.ch__rule {\n  margin-top: var(--s6);\n  height: 1px;\n  background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), transparent);\n}\n\n.ch__body {\n  min-width: 0;\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s12);\n}\n\n/* ---- Sticky card stack --------------------------------------------------\n   Every card is sticky at the SAME offset, so each comes to rest on the one\n   before it and the stack assembles itself as you scroll. The entire effect is\n   the equal `top` value — there is no JavaScript here at all.\n\n   Each card needs its own opaque background or the stack reads as a smear;\n   that is the one thing people get wrong when copying this. */\n.stack {\n  display: grid;\n  gap: var(--s8);\n}\n.stack__card {\n  position: sticky;\n  top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s8));\n  background-color: var(--surface);\n  border: 1px solid var(--border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-lg);\n  padding: var(--s8);\n  /* A hairline of the ground above each card so stacked edges stay readable. */\n  box-shadow: 0 -1px 0 0 var(--bg);\n}\n@media (min-width: 768px) {\n  .stack__card {\n    padding: var(--s12);\n  }\n}\n\n/* The stack is a scroll effect. Under reduced motion it is simply a list —\n   which is what it already is semantically, so nothing is lost. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .stack__card,\n  .ch__head {\n    position: static;\n  }\n}\n/* Sticky needs a real scroll context; without JS the layout is identical, so\n   no .no-js override is required here. */\n\n.stack__index {\n  font-family: var(--font-jetbrains-mono), ui-monospace, monospace;\n  font-size: var(--text-xs);\n  letter-spacing: 0.16em;\n  color: var(--accent);\n}\n.stack__title {\n  margin: var(--s3) 0 0;\n  font-size: var(--text-2xl);\n  letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);\n}\n.stack__body {\n  margin: var(--s4) 0 0;\n  color: var(--muted);\n  line-height: 1.65;\n  max-width: 62ch;\n}\n\n@media print {\n  .stack__card,\n  .ch__head {\n    position: static;\n  }\n}\n4c:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-phaseStack\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-story\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$9e\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"stack\",\"children\":[\"$L9f\",\"$La0\",\"$La1\",\"$La2\",\"$La3\",\"$La4\"]}]]}]\na5:Tdb3,\n.btn {\n  --btn-bg: transparent;\n  --btn-bg-hover: transparent;\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: transparent;\n  --btn-border-hover: transparent;\n\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: center;\n  gap: var(--s2);\n  border: 1px solid var(--btn-border);\n  border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  color: var(--btn-fg);\n  font-family: var(--font-inter-tight), var(--font-inter), ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;\n  font-weight: 500;\n  letter-spacing: -0.01em;\n  line-height: 1;\n  text-align: center;\n  text-decoration: none;\n  cursor: pointer;\n  /* ONLY colour transitions. A transform here would break the house rule. */\n  transition:\n    background-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out),\n    color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out);\n}\n.btn:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg-hover);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border-hover);\n  /* Falls back to the resting label colour, so no existing variant changes.\n     A variant whose hover fill moves far in lightness needs to move its label\n     too, or the hover state quietly fails contrast while the resting state\n     passes — which is the kind of thing an audit on static screenshots misses. */\n  color: var(--btn-fg-hover, var(--btn-fg));\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true'],\n.btn:disabled {\n  opacity: 0.45;\n  cursor: not-allowed;\n}\n.btn[aria-disabled='true']:hover,\n.btn:disabled:hover {\n  background-color: var(--btn-bg);\n  border-color: var(--btn-border);\n}\n\n/* ---- sizes. md and lg clear the 44x44 touch target. ---- */\n.btn--sm { min-height: 32px; padding-inline: var(--s3); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--md { min-height: 44px; min-width: 44px; padding-inline: var(--s4); font-size: var(--text-sm); }\n.btn--lg { min-height: 52px; min-width: 52px; padding-inline: var(--s6); font-size: var(--text-base); }\n\n.btn--full { width: 100%; }\n\n/* ---- variants ---- */\n.btn--primary {\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent);\n  --btn-fg: var(--accent-fg);\n  --btn-bg-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent);\n  --btn-border-hover: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 82%, var(--fg) 18%);\n}\n.theme-light .btn--primary {\n  /* On paper, --accent is the DARK copper (#A04F1A) because it has to pass\n     4.5:1 as link TEXT. As a large filled surface that same value reads muddy\n     brown, which is not what the brand is. A fill has a different contrast\n     problem from text: the requirement is on the LABEL against the fill, and\n     ink on vibrant copper measures 6.9:1 — comfortably clear. So the fill gets\n     the real brand copper and the label goes dark. Links and the focus ring\n     keep --accent and stay legible. */\n  --btn-bg: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-fg: var(--ink-900);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--accent-600);\n  --btn-fg-hover: var(--paper-50);\n  --btn-border: var(--accent-500);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--accent-600);\n}\n.btn--secondary {\n  --btn-fg: var(--fg);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--fg);\n}\n.btn--ghost {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--border);\n}\n.btn--ghost:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n.btn--danger-quiet {\n  --btn-fg: var(--muted-strong);\n  --btn-border: var(--border-strong);\n  --btn-bg-hover: var(--surface);\n  --btn-border-hover: var(--muted-strong);\n}\n.btn--danger-quiet:hover { color: var(--fg); }\n\n.btn__icon { display: inline-flex; flex: none; }\n4d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"sv-note\",\"style\":{\"marginTop\":\"var(--s8)\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"style\",null,{\"href\":\"envenox-button\",\"precedence\":\"default\",\"children\":\"$a5\"}],\"$La6\"]}]\n4f:[\"$\",\"figure\",null,{\"className\":\"dg dg-stackFig\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-stack\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 531 358\",\"preserveAspectRatio\":\"xMidYMin meet\",\"role\":\"img\",\"aria-label\":\"What lands in your inbox on a Penetration Testing engagement: 6 deliverables. 1, Technical report, written report. 2, Executive summary, live register. 3, Findings register as CSV and JSON, keyed for direct import into Jira, Linear or ServiceNow, csv + json. 4, Retest report within 30 days with a per-finding verified status, written report. 5, 90-minute debrief with the testers, live session. 6, Attestation letter suitable for customers, auditors and insurers, signed letter.\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"g\",\"Technical report — every finding with CVSS v4.0 vector, affected component, reproduction path, raw request/response evidence, and a remediation we would accept in code review\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheet\",\"x\":18,\"y\":18,\"width\":470,\"height\":92,\"rx\":6}],[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetSpine\",\"x\":18,\"y\":18,\"width\":3,\"height\":92}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetNum u-mono\",\"x\":36,\"y\":38,\"children\":\"01\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetTag\",\"x\":472,\"y\":38,\"textAnchor\":\"end\",\"children\":\"Written report\"}],[\"$\",\"text\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetTitle\",\"x\":36,\"y\":56,\"children\":\"Technical report\"}],[\"$\",\"line\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheetRule\",\"x1\":36,\"y1\":62,\"x2\":472,\"y2\":62}]]}],[\"$\",\"g\",\"Executive summary — two pages, written for a board, with the risk narrative and the three decisions that matter\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"rect\",null,{\"className\":\"dg-sheet\",\"x\":23,\"y\":64,\"width\